# docs/07-ONE-PAGE-DIRECTIVE.md §2: every route outside the four-route collapse is retired and
# 301s to /. Query strings are preserved automatically by the redirect syntax below; every rule
# is a single hop straight to /, never chained through another redirect first.
#
# None of the named paths below were ever built in this repository (confirmed against git
# history and docs/00-MASTER-BRIEF.md §10.5 "Future SEO pages" / §12.8 "Optional in first
# build") — they are retired-by-plan, not retired-by-deletion. Listed explicitly for a clear
# audit trail.
#
# No wildcard catch-all here: Cloudflare Pages applies _redirects rules unconditionally, before
# checking whether a real asset exists at that path (confirmed via `wrangler pages dev`), so a
# `/* / 301` rule matches every request including `/` itself and would 301-loop the entire site,
# homepage included. Unmatched paths fall through to Cloudflare Pages' standard 404 instead.
/about/                                 /  301
/project-standards/                     /  301
/service-area/                          /  301
/estate-cleanout-san-jose/              /  301
/property-cleanout-san-jose/            /  301
/vacant-home-cleaning-san-jose/         /  301
/hoarding-cleanup-san-jose/             /  301
/landlord-turnover-cleaning-san-jose/   /  301
